            "quotation": "The February increase in the goods and services deficit reflected a decrease in the goods deficit of $0.3 billion to $91.4 billion and a decrease in the services surplus of $1.6 billion to $22.5 billion."
          }
        ],
        "support_status": "not_independently_verified",
        "role": "support"
      },
      {
        "text": "The BEA attributes the deficit increase to decreases in the goods deficit and services surplus, yet both changes would narrow the deficit; the arithmetic (deficit up 1.9% to $68.9B) suggests the larger import growth ($7.1B) outpaced export growth, so the stated 'reflected' wording appears inconsistent with, or offset by, these components.",
